PROTOCOL = "# EURCHF H1 LONG Pass 8 — matched P32→P33 historical admission plan\n\nPredeclared 6 October 2026 after Pass7 review, before Pass8 code or long portfolio outcomes. **Candidate entry and RR are immutable.** This is a historical model comparison for the current 32-strategy registry using the available archived common cutoff; not actual live equity, an OOS test or permission to add orders.\n\n## One addition, twelve paired scenarios\n\nUse exactly the frozen long range 1.375/RR3 candidate, research ID EURCHF_H1_LONG_Q_L200_D025_R1375_PB0375_N12D2_RR3_RESEARCH_V1. Original range 1.50 long is an audit control only. The incumbent EURCHF short is EURCHF_H1_SHORT_PRIMARY_L060_D0075_SC035_PC075_RR3P50_V1 at RR3.50. No quality-short alternative, second-long choice, combination, threshold/RR/risk/filter/date/session search or automatic allocation ranking.\n\nSix P32 baselines: archived P31 plus the current original short, at two exit models ×10/20/40 ticks. Six P33 scenarios: add the one long using the same EURCHF model/cost as its paired baseline. Total 12 performance scenarios. Reproduce all existing six P32 controls before reporting additions; no using a favorable baseline cost against a different candidate cost. Both EURCHF strategies use the paired cost; older31archived strategy R/cost assumptions unchanged. Comparisons do not rerun universal broker costs.\n\nThe accompanying baseline JSON pins exact archived book/registry/six summaries/provenance, plus the verified long result SHA. P31 book SHA9d72e3af60e8a563a715eba2f123820f403e503e418b9f77b53219b70d882046;31 strategies / 3,332 completed trades. Existing P32 controls 3,391 completed trades,32 strategies. Verify alias mapping to supplied live registry, exact risk map and original short definition without silently modifying incumbent trades. This is the historical-model snapshot of the registered portfolio, not proof of every actual live acceptance.\n\n## Source and common cutoff\n\nReuse the confirmed pinned 137,819 H1 MID source and full-history confirmation gates for both exact EURCHF rules. Common portfolio cutoff 2026-09-20T18:29:00Z; requested beginning 2005-01-01T00:00Z. Only completed H1 candles at cutoff (137624 in previous admission) may support path exits. Recompute causal prefix features/paths and each model/cost replay; no use of future stop/target outcomes or selection of only trades that later closed. Preserve unresolved end positions with blank R/occupied state/allocated risk. Match prefix memberships to causally censored full-history signals; expose incomplete/after-cutoff bars. Do not extend archived31book to September30 or mix its equity horizon with full-history standalone statistics.\n\n## Joint EURCHF acceptance\n\nFreeze non-hedging assumption from user's last executor preview (false) and supplied executor REQUIRE_HEDGING_FOR_OPPOSITE_OVERLAP=True. This affects EURCHF directly now that both directions exist. Existing forced AUDJPY gate stays as represented in its archived accepted book; older31streams unchanged because this addition introduces no EURCHF position into another instrument's acceptance and no shared global acceptance cap is modeled. If actual additional/global gates or acceptance-dependent conversion/position limits are discovered, require adequate raw streams and revised pre-outcome scope instead of silently treating accepted book as sufficient.\n\nRebuild raw-qualified short and long streams; do not merge only their accepted standalone trades. Handle per-ID p0, cost-invalid geometry, open end state and opposite-direction gate in true chronological order. Block an attempted direction if the opposite EURCHF strategy remains open; no implicit netting or incumbent closure. Blocked/invalid entries do not claim occupancy; subsequent qualified signals may be accepted. Both directions can lose would-be trades relative to standalone. Report every blocked/recovered/displaced incumbent/candidate raw identity and eventual outcomes separately, including proof that it was raw-qualified and its blocking counterpart was active.\n\nPreserve exact prior execution event timing: EXIT before ENTRY at same actual timestamp, original lexical ID/stable row tie order in portfolio sizing, and previous source-index convention permitting an exit-candle *signal* whose nominal entry is that candle's close. Use the actual open-gap exit time where applicable; do not retrospectively release occupancy for a signal formed earlier than its allowed execution time. Any translation between source-index signal eligibility and portfolio-entry clock must be explicit and tested on synthetic same-bar/tie/gap/end cases. The accepted baseline with only short must match the previously confirmed p0 ledger exactly.\n\n## Accounting and required evidence\n\nInitial model equity 100 arbitrary units, fixed candidate 1% of then-realized equity, existing 1% except EUR_JPY_M15_SHORT0.75%. No risk sweep. Inherit exact old entry-sizing, EXIT/ENTRY tie, realized-equity compounding, closed-DD and nominal open-risk-floor functions with full controls; no invented global cap. Report that nominal floor is not marked NAV/intratrade DD or a gap-loss bound. Account-currency conversion, broker rounding/financing and measured spreads are not supplied by archived dimensionless R.\n\nRequired exports: source/registry/book hashes, complete expected-versus-actual P32 baseline ledgers and equity events, both full-history and causal cutoff streams, raw memberships, joint per-ID/pair gate/invalid/open audit, all accepted/rejected differences, every sized event, cash identities, candidate versus changed-short versus other-incumbent resizing attribution. Match all baseline summary/event/monthly/period/rolling reports to trusted Pass13 originals (whose returned-file parity was previously established), not aggregate counts alone.\n\nReport paired P32/P33 common-window return/equity/CAGR, closed and nominal-floor DD, concurrency/allocated open risk/gross EUR and CHF involvement, every calendar/era/latest 1/2/3/5/10 year/CHF period, zero-inclusive monthly and complete-month 12/24/36M rolling outcomes. Partial September excluded from complete-month rolling as before. Entries[a,b), realized cash exits(a,b]. Include weak-window and deepest-DD strategy cash contributions, all matched rolling deltas, empty candidate periods and realized/censored exposures. Distinguish added long R from net portfolio effect after lost/recovered short entries and balance resizing.\n\nAny source/frozen-ledger/raw chronology/baseline/registry/cash/report parity failure gives error-only diagnostics, no partial admission output. Keep all twelve scenarios visible. Review return together with drawdown/short displacement/recent/rolling/exposure, no automatic score. Classification after user returns results: rejected, retained for research or provisionally historically admissible under this exact model. Portfolio feedback never reopens tuning; an unhelpful addition parks this Q chain. Prospective read-only execution evidence and any activation remain later separately authorized stages.\n\nNo Pass8 code, run or outcome exists when this plan is frozen; no live file/account/broker/quote/order/deployment changes.\n\n\n## Pass8 implementation choices fixed before new long-portfolio outcomes\n\nThis standalone runner embeds the full137819H1 source, original LONG Pass7 reference, selected PRIMARY short controls and P31 completed book from the trusted Pass13 archive. Only PRIMARY short is replayed; no D1 quality or rejected frequency arms. All12 LONG full-history controls and6 PRIMARY short ledgers/raw features are frozen checks. All six P32 summary, full accepted cutoff ledger, every equity event, overlap, monthly, period and rolling report must reproduce typed fields/order before any P33 arm. Source/embedded controls/frozen baseline/spec/registry/cash failures publish error-only diagnostics and remove stale valid results. No fetching broker history or live/account requests.\n\nOwn-ID p0 retains the historical source-index eligibility rule (new signal index>=previous exit source index). Opposite EURCHF gating uses actual simulated exit time at nominal entry clock; an exit at exactly that time releases the pair before entry. Thus an opening-gap exit can release the OTHER direction at that opening clock while the same-ID preceding-bar signal is still rejected under its stricter preserved source-index p0. This explicit translation preserves prior standalone ledgers. No pair exposure overlap is permitted. Invalid/blocked attempts never own a position. Exact entry ties use lexical strategy ID then signal index, matching the declared portfolio event convention; this is a deterministic historical assumption, not a claim about live request arrival.\n\nFor each common cutoff build RAW qualified short and long streams causally; reconstruct paths from completed prefix only. Report censored full/prefix membership/ledger parity, standalone controls, all joint gate attempts with blocker identities and actual times, every retained/added/recovered/removed acceptance. Same retained signal must preserve geometry/outcome (accepted sequence can change). Changed short entries are distinguished from candidate long R and other31 equity resizing. Every entry risk and exit cash event is exported. EUR/CHF involvement is gross allocated nominal risk, not hedge offsets, currency delta or diversification evidence.\n\nLegacy portfolio `source=CANDIDATE` means any EURCHF trade in the preserved P32 accounting contract. New outputs add `portfolio_component`/long/short/other31 fields to disambiguate; do not read the legacy source label as LONG. Candidate_* legacy summary/interval fields also count both EURCHF directions in P33. Use explicit long_* and short_* fields. Initial100 are arbitrary model units. Archived compounded totals and CAGR are model arithmetic, not achievable returns or actual current account equity. The other31 source is a frozen completed accepted book, with old costs/gates already embedded; it cannot prove unprovided historical open exposures or recreate all live acceptance. Yearlong or other long exposures do not include financing in this model.\n\nExactly12 scenarios,6 paired deltas.261 monthly intervals per case (September2026partial),35 calendar/era/recent/CHF periods, complete-month12/24/36M widths with249/237/225 windows per case, total8532rolling rows/4266paired rows. PartialSeptember excluded from complete rolling. Entry intervals[a,b), realized cash(a,b]; endpoint balances include all exits at endpoint. Zero-inclusive candidate activity and long open exposure explicit. Preserve all negative/weak/unchanged intervals, no automated ranking or admission. Cash attribution to new long/changed short/other31 resizing is exact, not naive summedR; performance percentages use each scenario's realized starting balance. Closed-DD and balance-minus-allocated-risk nominal floor are not intratrade NAV/financing/gap-loss guarantees.\n\nRead-only Python3.10 standard library. Run python app.py, /status COMPLETE then /results. Optional --run-once --output-dir ./long_admission_results; optional EURCHF_LONG_PASS8_OUTPUT_DIR in dedicated research folder. No packages, credentials or live activation variables. GET/HEAD only. One process on Windows; Linux advisory output lock. This reuses the confirmed signal/accounting engine, not a new independent implementation or untouched OOS evidence. Current live SHORT/executor/probe are not modified. Subsequent review can reject/retain-for-research/provisionally accept only under this historical model; live approval remains separate.\n"
README = '# Run EURCHF H1 LONG Pass8 portfolio comparison\n\n1. Save EURCHF_H1_LONG_PASS8_P32_TO_P33_ADMISSION.py as **app.py** in a separate research service.\n2. Run `python app.py` (Python3.10+, standard library, no packages/credentials/live variables).\n3. Wait for `/status` to show `status: COMPLETE` and `complete: true`.\n4. Download `/results` and return **EURCHF_H1_LONG_PASS8_P32_TO_P33_ADMISSION_RESULTS.zip**. If ERROR, return its diagnostics.\n\nLocal batch: `python app.py --run-once --output-dir ./long_admission_results`.\nOptional EURCHF_LONG_PASS8_OUTPUT_DIR chooses a dedicated output folder; prior study ZIP/status there are replaced. HOST/PORT(default8000) and WSGI app:app / app:application supported. One process on Windows.\n\nExactly6 current32-registry historical baselines and6 additions of the frozen original LONG RR3. Both EURCHF directions use matched1/2/4pip costs and both exit models. No strategy tuning or automated selection. Uses full2005–September2026 source for standalone controls; both portfolios use the archived20September2026common cutoff. Other31 completed trades unchanged. Raw joint EURCHF replay models own p0 and nonhedging opposite gate, rejected/recovered/displaced trades, sized cash events, drawdown/concurrency/exposure, calendar/recent/zero-inclusive rolling and exact paired cash contribution.\n\nAll source/reference data embedded. Current live services unchanged; no orders. This is a historical model comparison using arbitrary initial100 units and a frozen accepted incumbent book, not actual account equity, untouched OOS or live approval. Read explicit long_/short_/other31 fields for attribution; legacy candidate_* means all EURCHF. Financing/conversion/measured broker spread and intratrade NAV are not modeled.\n'



def fingerprint(data):
    return hashlib.sha256(data).hexdigest()


def stamp(t):
    return t.astimezone(UTC).isoformat(timespec='seconds').replace('+00:00','Z')


def parse_stamp(value):
    return datetime.fromisoformat(value.replace('Z','+00:00'))


def unpack(payload, digest):
    plain = zlib.decompress(base64.b85decode(payload))
    if fingerprint(plain) != digest:
        raise ValueError('Embedded input checksum failed')
    return plain


def csv_bytes(records, columns=None):
    records = list(records)
    if columns is None:
        columns = list(records[0]) if records else ['no_rows']
    stream = io.StringIO(newline='')
    writer = csv.DictWriter(stream,fieldnames=columns,lineterminator='\n',extrasaction='raise')
    writer.writeheader(); writer.writerows(records)
    return stream.getvalue().encode()


def json_bytes(value):
    return (json.dumps(value,indent=2,allow_nan=False)+'\n').encode()


def ledger_digest(records):
    # Historical canonical serialization contract, not copied strategy logic.
    digest = hashlib.sha256()
    for record in records:
        canonical = {field:record[field] for field in LEDGER_FIELDS}
        digest.update((json.dumps(canonical,sort_keys=True,separators=(',',':'),allow_nan=False)+'\n').encode())
    return digest.hexdigest()


def parse_reference_record(record):
    result = {}
    for field in LEDGER_FIELDS:
        value = record[field]
        result[field] = (None if value in ('',None) else int(value) if field in INT_FIELDS else float(value) if field in FLOAT_FIELDS else value)
    return result


def load_candles(raw):
    data = list(csv.DictReader(io.StringIO(raw.decode())))
    if not data or tuple(data[0]) != ('time','open','high','low','close'):
        raise ValueError('Unexpected candle schema')
    candles = []
    for row in data:
        values = tuple(float(row[k]) for k in ('open','high','low','close'))
        t = parse_stamp(row['time'])
        op,hi,lo,cl = values
        if not all(math.isfinite(v) and v>0 for v in values) or lo>min(op,cl) or hi<max(op,cl) or hi<lo:
            raise ValueError('Invalid source OHLC')
        if not BEGIN<=t<CUTOFF or (candles and t<=candles[-1][0]):
            raise ValueError('Invalid source chronology/cutoff')
        candles.append((t,op,hi,lo,cl))
    return candles


def source_digest(candles):
    text = '\n'.join(','.join([stamp(c[0])]+[format(v,'.5f') for v in c[1:]]) for c in candles)
    return fingerprint(text.encode())


def is_engulf(previous, current):
    return (previous[4]<previous[1] and current[4]>current[1]
            and current[1]<=previous[4] and current[4]>=previous[1])


def wilder_series(candles):
    ranges = [None]
    for old,new in zip(candles,candles[1:]):
        ranges.append(max(new[2]-new[3],abs(new[2]-old[4]),abs(new[3]-old[4])))
    atr = [None]*len(candles)
    if len(candles)>=15:
        atr[14] = sum(ranges[1:15])/14
        for index in range(15,len(candles)):
            atr[index] = (13*atr[index-1]+ranges[index])/14
    return atr


def extract_features(candles):
    atr = wilder_series(candles)
    # Heap stores only already observed lows. Expiration enforces the exact
    # previous200 observed candles and excludes the current candle.
    heap = []
    features = []
    for i,candle in enumerate(candles):
        if i:
            heapq.heappush(heap,(candles[i-1][3],i-1))
        while heap and heap[0][1]<i-200:
            heapq.heappop(heap)
        if i<200 or not is_engulf(candles[i-1],candle):
            continue
        a,p = atr[i],atr[i-1]
        if a is None or p is None or a<=0 or p<=0:
            raise ValueError('Nonpositive ATR after warmup')
        low = heap[0][0]
        features.append(dict(signal_index=i,signal=stamp(candle[0]),entry=stamp(candle[0]+HOUR),
            atr14=a,body_atr=(candle[4]-candle[1])/a,range_atr=(candle[2]-candle[3])/a,
            previous_low_200=low,abs_distance_atr_200=abs(candle[3]-low)/a,
            previous_body_atr=abs(candles[i-1][4]-candles[i-1][1])/p,
            decline_12_atr=(candles[i-13][4]-candles[i-1][4])/p))
    return features


def entry_qualifies(feature, minimum_range):
    return (feature['abs_distance_atr_200']<=0.25 and feature['body_atr']>=0.75
            and feature['range_atr']>=minimum_range and feature['previous_body_atr']>=0.375
            and feature['decline_12_atr']>=2.0)


def raw_digest(indices, candles):
    return fingerprint('\n'.join(stamp(candles[i][0]) for i in indices).encode())


def resolve_touch(candle,stop,target,model):
    t,op,hi,lo,_ = candle
    hit_stop,hit_target = lo<=stop,hi>=target
    if not (hit_stop or hit_target):
        return None
    both = int(hit_stop and hit_target)
    if model=='SCREEN_PARITY':
        choose_target = (hi-op)<(op-lo) if both else hit_target
        return (target if choose_target else stop, t+HOUR,
                'TARGET' if choose_target else 'STOP', both,0,0)
    if model!='STOP_FIRST_GAP_STRESS':
        raise ValueError('Unknown exit model')
    if op<=stop:
        return (op,t,'STOP_GAP' if op<stop else 'STOP',both,int(op<stop),0)
    if op>=target:
        return (target,t,'TARGET_GAP_CAPPED',both,0,1)
    return (stop if hit_stop else target,t+HOUR,'STOP' if hit_stop else 'TARGET',both,0,0)


def construct_paths(candles, signal_indices):
    paths = {}
    for i in signal_indices:
        ref = candles[i][4]
        stop = candles[i][3]-10*TICK
        target = ref+RR*(ref-stop)
        common = dict(signal_index=i,signal=stamp(candles[i][0]),entry=stamp(candles[i][0]+HOUR),
            reference_entry=ref,stop=stop,target=target,
            next_open=candles[i+1][1] if i+1<len(candles) else None,
            next_candle_delay_hours=(candles[i+1][0]-candles[i][0]-HOUR).total_seconds()/3600 if i+1<len(candles) else None)
        for model in MODELS:
            result = None
            for j in range(i+1,len(candles)):
                result = resolve_touch(candles[j],stop,target,model)
                if result is not None:
                    price,exit_time,reason,dual,gap_stop,gap_target = result
                    paths[model,i] = dict(common,execution_model=model,exit_index=j,exit=stamp(exit_time),exit_price=price,
                        reason=reason,dual_touch=dual,gap_stop=gap_stop,gap_target=gap_target)
                    break
            if result is None:
                paths[model,i] = dict(common,execution_model=model,exit_index=None,exit=None,exit_price=None,
                    reason='OPEN_AT_DATA_END',dual_touch=0,gap_stop=0,gap_target=0)
    return paths


def entry_problem(path,cost):
    fill = path['reference_entry']+cost*TICK
    if parse_stamp(path['entry'])>=CUTOFF:
        return fill,'ENTRY_AT_OR_AFTER_CUTOFF'
    if not 0<path['stop']<fill<path['target']:
        return fill,'INVALID_FILL_STOP_TARGET_GEOMETRY'
    return fill,None


def simulate(config,model,cost,indices,paths):
    ledger,invalid,blocked = [],[],[]
    unavailable_before = -1
    for i in indices:
        p = paths[model,i]
        if i<unavailable_before:
            blocked.append(dict(config_id=config,execution_model=model,cost_ticks=cost,signal_index=i,reason='P0_OCCUPIED'))
            continue
        fill,problem = entry_problem(p,cost)
        if problem:
            invalid.append(dict(config_id=config,execution_model=model,cost_ticks=cost,signal_index=i,reason=problem))
            continue
        risk = fill-p['stop']
        value = None if p['exit_price'] is None else (p['exit_price']-fill)/risk
        row = {k:p[k] for k in ('signal_index','exit_index','signal','entry','exit','reference_entry','stop','target','exit_price','reason')}
        row.update(config_id=config,execution_model=model,cost_ticks=cost,accepted_sequence=len(ledger)+1,
                   historical_fill=fill,risk_price=risk,r=value)
        ledger.append(row)
        unavailable_before = p['exit_index'] if p['exit_index'] is not None else math.inf
    return ledger,invalid,blocked


def return_stats(values):
    values = [v for v in values if v is not None]
    balance,peak,dd,streak,max_streak = 0.,0.,0.,0,0
    for v in values:
        balance+=v;peak=max(peak,balance);dd=min(dd,balance-peak)
        streak = streak+1 if v<0 else 0;max_streak=max(streak,max_streak)
    gains=sum(v for v in values if v>0);loss=-sum(v for v in values if v<0)
    return dict(closed_trades=len(values),wins=sum(v>0 for v in values),losses=sum(v<0 for v in values),
        total_r=sum(values),max_closed_dd_r=dd,max_losing_streak=max_streak,
        expectancy_r=sum(values)/len(values) if values else None,profit_factor=gains/loss if loss else None)


def case_stats(config,model,cost,indices,ledger,invalid,blocked,candles):
    return dict(config_id=config,execution_model=model,cost_ticks=cost,rr=RR,
        raw_signals=len(indices),raw_signal_sha256=raw_digest(indices,candles),
        accepted_ledger_sha256=ledger_digest(ledger),
        accepted_signal_set_sha256=fingerprint(','.join(str(i) for i in sorted(r['signal_index'] for r in ledger)).encode()),
        open_at_data_end=sum(r['r'] is None for r in ledger),invalid_unblocked_entries=len(invalid),p0_blocked_signals=len(blocked),
        **return_stats([r['r'] for r in ledger]))


def close_enough(a,b):
    if a is None or b is None:
        return a is None and b is None
    if isinstance(a,(int,float)) and not isinstance(a,bool):
        return isinstance(b,(int,float)) and math.isfinite(float(b)) and math.isclose(a,b,rel_tol=1e-12,abs_tol=1e-10)
    return a==b


def gate(checks,label,expected,actual):
    okay = close_enough(expected,actual)
    checks.append(dict(check=label,status='PASS' if okay else 'FAIL',expected=expected,actual=actual))
    if not okay:
        raise ValueError('Confirmation gate failed: '+label)


def field_check(report,case,actual,reference,fields):
    if len(actual)!=len(reference):
        report.append(dict(case=case,row_sequence='',field='row_count',expected=len(reference),actual=len(actual),status='FAIL'))
        raise ValueError('Reference row count mismatch: '+case)
    for sequence,(observed,expected) in enumerate(zip(actual,reference),1):
        for field in fields:
            a,b = observed[field],expected[field]
            okay = close_enough(b,a)
            report.append(dict(case=case,row_sequence=sequence,field=field,expected=b,actual=a,status='PASS' if okay else 'FAIL'))
            if not okay:
                raise ValueError('Field parity failed: '+case+'/'+str(sequence)+'/'+field)


def month_shift(t,delta):
    y,m = divmod(t.year*12+t.month-1+delta,12)
    return datetime(y,m+1,1,tzinfo=UTC)


def period_calendar():
    windows=[]
    for year in range(2005,2027):
        windows.append(('YEAR_'+str(year),'calendar',datetime(year,1,1,tzinfo=UTC),min(datetime(year+1,1,1,tzinfo=UTC),CUTOFF)))
    for a,b in ((2005,2010),(2010,2016),(2016,2022),(2022,2027)):
        windows.append((f'ERA_{a}_{b-1}','era',datetime(a,1,1,tzinfo=UTC),min(datetime(b,1,1,tzinfo=UTC),CUTOFF)))
    for years in (1,2,3,5,10):
        windows.append((f'LATEST_{years}Y','recent',CUTOFF.replace(year=CUTOFF.year-years),CUTOFF))
    windows.extend([('CHF_PRE_FLOOR','policy_diagnostic',BEGIN,datetime(2011,9,6,tzinfo=UTC)),
        ('CHF_FLOOR_PERIOD','policy_diagnostic',datetime(2011,9,6,tzinfo=UTC),datetime(2015,1,15,tzinfo=UTC)),
        ('CHF_2015_01_15','policy_diagnostic',datetime(2015,1,15,tzinfo=UTC),datetime(2015,1,16,tzinfo=UTC)),
        ('CHF_AFTER_2015_01_15','policy_diagnostic',datetime(2015,1,16,tzinfo=UTC),CUTOFF)])
    return windows


def timed_rows(ledger):
    return [(parse_stamp(r['entry']),parse_stamp(r['exit']) if r['exit'] else None,r['r'],r) for r in ledger]


def window_results(timed,start,end):
    cohort=[r for r in timed if start<=r[0]<end]
    realized=[r for r in timed if r[1] is not None and start<r[1]<=end]
    realized.sort(key=lambda r:(r[1],r[3]['signal_index']))
    stats=return_stats([r[2] for r in realized])
    return dict(entries=len(cohort),entry_cohort_closed_trades=sum(r[2] is not None for r in cohort),
        entry_cohort_r=sum(r[2] for r in cohort if r[2] is not None),entry_cohort_unresolved=sum(r[2] is None for r in cohort),
        realized_exits=len(realized),realized_r=stats['total_r'],realized_closed_dd_r=stats['max_closed_dd_r'],
        open_at_start=sum(r[0]<start and (r[1] is None or r[1]>start) for r in timed),
        open_at_end=sum(r[0]<end and (r[1] is None or r[1]>end) for r in timed),zero_entry=int(not cohort))


def reporting(ledgers):
    monthly,periods,rolling,influence,events,activity=[],[],[],[],[],[]
    months=[month_shift(BEGIN,i) for i in range(262)]
    for (cid,model,cost),ledger in ledgers.items():
        tag=dict(config_id=cid,execution_model=model,cost_ticks=cost,rr=RR)
        timed=timed_rows(ledger)
        per_month=[]
        for a,b in zip(months,months[1:]):
            result=window_results(timed,a,b);per_month.append(result['entries'])
            monthly.append(dict(tag,month=a.strftime('%Y-%m'),start=stamp(a),end=stamp(b),**result))
        for name,kind,a,b in period_calendar():
            periods.append(dict(tag,period=name,period_type=kind,start=stamp(a),end=stamp(b),partial_calendar_year=int(kind=='calendar' and b.month!=1),**window_results(timed,a,b)))
        for span in (12,24,36):
            for i in range(262-span):
                a,b=months[i],months[i+span]
                rolling.append(dict(tag,window_months=span,start=stamp(a),end=stamp(b),**window_results(timed,a,b)))
        wins=sorted([r['r'] for r in ledger if r['r'] is not None and r['r']>0],reverse=True)
        influence.append(dict(tag,largest_winner_r=wins[0] if wins else None,top_three_winners_r=sum(wins[:3]),
            descriptive_total_less_top_three_r=sum(r['r'] for r in ledger if r['r'] is not None)-sum(wins[:3]),
            warning='Descriptive concentration only; no trade deletion or alternate backtest'))
        longest=run=0
        for n in per_month:
            run=run+1 if n==0 else 0;longest=max(longest,run)
        times=[r[0] for r in timed]
        holding=[(r[1]-r[0]).total_seconds()/3600 for r in timed if r[1] is not None]
        empty_years=sum(not any(r[0].year==year for r in timed) for year in range(2005,2026))
        activity.append(dict(tag,accepted_entries=len(ledger),zero_entry_months=sum(n==0 for n in per_month),max_consecutive_zero_entry_months=longest,
            zero_entry_complete_years=empty_years,median_holding_hours=statistics.median(holding) if holding else None,max_holding_hours=max(holding) if holding else None,
            maximum_inter_entry_gap_days=max(((b-a).total_seconds()/86400 for a,b in zip(times,times[1:])),default=None),
            leading_no_entry_days=(times[0]-BEGIN).total_seconds()/86400 if times else None,trailing_no_entry_days=(CUTOFF-times[-1]).total_seconds()/86400 if times else None))
        a=datetime(2015,1,15,tzinfo=UTC);b=a+timedelta(days=1)
        for entry,exit_time,value,row in timed:
            entered=a<=entry<b;exited=exit_time is not None and a<=exit_time<b;held=entry<a and (exit_time is None or exit_time>=a)
            if entered or exited or held:
                events.append(dict(tag,signal_index=row['signal_index'],entry=row['entry'],exit=row['exit'],entered_on_event_day=int(entered),exited_on_event_day=int(exited),held_across_event_day_start=int(held),eventual_r=value,outcome=row['reason'],attribution_warning='Exposure only; no event-removal counterfactual'))
    return monthly,periods,rolling,influence,events,activity


def synthetic_checks():
    checks=[]
    def check(label,value):
        if not value:raise ValueError('Software check failed: '+label)
        checks.append(dict(check=label,status='PASS',evidence='SYNTHETIC_SOFTWARE_ONLY'))
    d=datetime(2005,1,1,tzinfo=UTC)
    prev=(d,1.2,1.3,1.0,1.1);cur=(d+HOUR,1.1,1.3,1.0,1.2)
    check('Engulf equality qualifies',is_engulf(prev,cur))
    check('Previous doji rejected',not is_engulf((d,1.1,1.3,1.,1.1),cur))
    check('Current doji rejected',not is_engulf(prev,(d+HOUR,1.1,1.3,1.,1.1)))
    feat=dict(abs_distance_atr_200=.25,body_atr=.75,range_atr=1.375,previous_body_atr=.375,decline_12_atr=2.)
    check('Inclusive candidate thresholds',entry_qualifies(feat,1.375))
    check('Different fixed range controls',not entry_qualifies(feat,1.5))
    for key,val in [('abs_distance_atr_200',.251),('body_atr',.749),('range_atr',1.374),('previous_body_atr',.374),('decline_12_atr',1.999)]:
        f=dict(feat);f[key]=val;check('Reject failing '+key,not entry_qualifies(f,1.375))
    dual=(d,1.5,2.1,.9,1.5)
    check('Stress dual touch stop',resolve_touch(dual,1.,2.,MODELS[1])[2]=='STOP')
    check('Screen tie stop',resolve_touch((d,1.5,2.,1.,1.5),1.,2.,MODELS[0])[2]=='STOP')
    check('Screen nearest-open target',resolve_touch((d,1.8,2.,1.,1.8),1.,2.,MODELS[0])[2]=='TARGET')
    gap=resolve_touch((d,.8,1.1,.7,.9),1.,2.,MODELS[1])
    check('Stop gap price/time',gap[0]==.8 and gap[1]==d and gap[2]=='STOP_GAP')
    check('Target gap capped',resolve_touch((d,2.2,2.3,2.1,2.2),1.,2.,MODELS[1])[0]==2.)
    check('No barrier returns none',resolve_touch((d,1.5,1.8,1.2,1.5),1.,2.,MODELS[1]) is None)
    b=[(d+HOUR*i,1.,1.1,.9,1.) for i in range(17)];a=wilder_series(b)
    check('ATR full seed availability',a[13] is None and math.isclose(a[14],.2,abs_tol=1e-12) and math.isclose(a[16],.2,abs_tol=1e-12))
    p=dict(reference_entry=1.1,stop=1.,target=1.4,entry=stamp(d),signal=stamp(d-HOUR),exit_index=2,exit=stamp(d+HOUR),exit_price=1.,reason='STOP',signal_index=0)
    paths={(MODELS[1],i):dict(p,signal_index=i) for i in range(4)}
    ledger,invalid,blocked=simulate('test',MODELS[1],10,[0,1,2],paths)
    check('P0 blocks before exit, permits exit index',[r['signal_index'] for r in ledger]==[0,2] and len(blocked)==1)
    paths[MODELS[1],0]=dict(p,exit_index=None,exit=None,exit_price=None,reason='OPEN_AT_DATA_END')
    ledger,_,blocked=simulate('test',MODELS[1],10,[0,1,2],paths)
    check('Unresolved occupies p0 and R blank',len(ledger)==1 and ledger[0]['r'] is None and len(blocked)==2)
    paths[MODELS[1],0]=dict(p,target=1.10005)
    ledger,invalid,_=simulate('test',MODELS[1],10,[0,1],paths)
    check('Invalid geometry does not occupy',len(invalid)==1 and ledger[0]['signal_index']==1)
    check('Cutoff rejected',entry_problem(dict(p,entry=stamp(CUTOFF)),10)[1]=='ENTRY_AT_OR_AFTER_CUTOFF')
    check('Closed DD and losing streak',return_stats([2.,-1.,-1.,3.,-1.])['max_closed_dd_r']==-2. and return_stats([2.,-1.,-1.,3.,-1.])['max_losing_streak']==2)
    try:resolve_touch(dual,1.,2.,'BAD')
    except ValueError:check('Unknown model rejects',True)
    else:check('Unknown model rejects',False)
    return checks


def build_long_control_reports(checks,fields):
    source=unpack(SOURCE_B85,SOURCE_BYTE_SHA)
    spec_data=unpack(SPEC_B85,SPEC_BYTE_SHA)
    reference_data=unpack(REFERENCE_B85,REFERENCE_BYTE_SHA)
    spec=json.loads(spec_data);refs=json.loads(reference_data)
    gate(checks,'Frozen specification version','EURCHF_H1_LONG_PASS7_FROZEN_CONFIRMATION_INPUTS_V1_2026_10_06',spec['version'])
    gate(checks,'Fixed frozen rules/costs/models/RR',[CANDIDATE,CONTROL,RR,list(COSTS),list(MODELS)],[spec['candidate_parent_id'],spec['audit_reference_parent_id'],spec['rr'],spec['execution']['cost_ticks'],spec['execution']['models']])
    candles=load_candles(source)
    gate(checks,'All full-history candles',137819,len(candles))
    gate(checks,'Full source canonical hash',spec['source']['canonical_sha256'],source_digest(candles))
    gate(checks,'Original source CSV byte hash',spec['source']['source_csv_sha256'],fingerprint(source))
    gate(checks,'First candle','2005-01-02T18:00:00Z',stamp(candles[0][0]))
    gate(checks,'Last candle','2026-09-30T23:00:00Z',stamp(candles[-1][0]))
    features=extract_features(candles)
    gate(checks,'Raw engulf full-history count',9781,len(features))
    field_check(fields,'FULL_RAW_FEATURES',features,refs['features'],FEATURE_FIELDS)
    for prefix in (205,64321,137805):
        short=extract_features(candles[:prefix]); full=[r for r in features if r['signal_index']<prefix]
        gate(checks,'Feature prefix causality '+str(prefix),fingerprint(json_bytes(full)),fingerprint(json_bytes(short)))
    populations={cid:[f['signal_index'] for f in features if entry_qualifies(f,threshold)] for cid,threshold,_ in RULES}
    for cid,indices in populations.items():
        gate(checks,'Complete raw membership '+cid,refs['populations'][cid],indices)
    paths=construct_paths(candles,sorted(set(i for p in populations.values() for i in p)))
    pathrows=sorted(paths.values(),key=lambda p:(p['execution_model'],p['signal_index']))
    field_check(fields,'FROZEN_PATHS',pathrows,refs['paths'],tuple(pathrows[0]))
    ledgers={}; summaries=[];invalid=[];blocked=[]
    for cid,_,_ in RULES:
        for model in MODELS:
            for cost in COSTS:
                key=(cid,model,cost);case=cid+'|'+model+'|'+str(cost)
                ledger,bad,occupied=simulate(cid,model,cost,populations[cid],paths)
                reference=[parse_reference_record(r) for r in refs['ledgers'][case]]
                field_check(fields,case,ledger,reference,LEDGER_FIELDS)
                summary=case_stats(cid,model,cost,populations[cid],ledger,bad,occupied,candles)
                expectation=next(e for e in spec['expected_cases'] if (e['config_id'],e['execution_model'],e['cost_ticks'])==key)
                for field,value in expectation.items():
                    gate(checks,case+' / '+field,value,summary[field])
                ledgers[key]=ledger;summaries.append(summary);invalid.extend(bad);blocked.extend(occupied)
    gate(checks,'All 12 model/cost cases',12,len(summaries))
    gate(checks,'All complete accepted rows',462,sum(len(l) for l in ledgers.values()))
    monthly,periods,rolling,influence,events,activity=reporting(ledgers)
    gate(checks,'Monthly zero-inclusive universe',3132,len(monthly))
    gate(checks,'Period universe',420,len(periods))
    gate(checks,'Rolling zero-inclusive universe',8568,len(rolling))
    perioddefs=[dict(period=n,period_type=k,start=stamp(a),end=stamp(b),entry_interval='[start,end)',exit_cash_interval='(start,end]') for n,k,a,b in period_calendar()]
    gaps=[dict(previous=stamp(a[0]),next=stamp(b[0]),elapsed_hours=(b[0]-a[0]).total_seconds()/3600,missing_clock_hours=(b[0]-a[0]).total_seconds()/3600-1,warning='Observed gap; not necessarily missing market candles') for a,b in zip(candles,candles[1:]) if b[0]-a[0]>HOUR]
    accepted=[dict(rr=RR,**r) for ledger in ledgers.values() for r in ledger]
    payload={'source_candles.csv':source,'frozen_specification.json':spec_data,'expected_reference_package.json':reference_data,
        'summary.csv':csv_bytes(summaries),'accepted_ledgers.csv':csv_bytes(accepted,['rr']+list(LEDGER_FIELDS)),
        'raw_signal_features.csv':csv_bytes(features),'raw_signal_membership.csv':csv_bytes([dict(config_id=cid,signal_index=i) for cid,p in populations.items() for i in p]),
        'signal_trade_paths.csv':csv_bytes(pathrows),'parity_checks.csv':csv_bytes(checks),'field_by_field_parity.csv':csv_bytes(fields),
        'software_checks.csv':csv_bytes(synthetic_checks()),'monthly_results.csv':csv_bytes(monthly),'period_results.csv':csv_bytes(periods),
        'period_definitions.csv':csv_bytes(perioddefs),'rolling_windows.csv':csv_bytes(rolling),'influence.csv':csv_bytes(influence),'activity.csv':csv_bytes(activity),
        'invalid_entries.csv':csv_bytes(invalid,['config_id','execution_model','cost_ticks','signal_index','reason']),
        'blocked_signals.csv':csv_bytes(blocked,['config_id','execution_model','cost_ticks','signal_index','reason']),
        'open_at_data_end.csv':csv_bytes([r for r in accepted if r['r'] is None],['rr']+list(LEDGER_FIELDS)),
        'chf_event_exposure.csv':csv_bytes(events,['config_id','execution_model','cost_ticks','rr','signal_index','entry','exit','entered_on_event_day','exited_on_event_day','held_across_event_day_start','eventual_r','outcome','attribution_warning']),
        'data_gaps.csv':csv_bytes(gaps),'coverage.csv':csv_bytes([dict(pair='EUR_CHF',side='BUY',timeframe='H1',price_type='MID',candles=len(candles),first=stamp(candles[0][0]),last=stamp(candles[-1][0]),requested_start=stamp(BEGIN),end_exclusive=stamp(CUTOFF),warmup_bars=200,sha256=source_digest(candles),dataset_kind='HISTORICAL_OANDA_MID_PINNED_SNAPSHOT')]),
        'protocol.md':PROTOCOL.encode(),'README.md':README.encode()}
    return payload,dict(candles=len(candles),raw_engulf_signals=len(features),cases=len(summaries),accepted_rows=len(accepted),parity_checks=len(checks),field_checks=len(fields),source_sha256=source_digest(candles))



